cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  MTPS-C: preregistered conformal prediction for chaotic
  three-body systems
message: >-
  If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata
  below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Peñafiel González
    given-names: Joaquín
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0005-2614-9393
    country: CL
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/joaquinpenafiel/conformal-prediction-three-body
abstract: >-
  A preregistered experimental program that characterises the
  operating domain of a conformal prediction instrument for
  chaotic three-body systems. Coverage is calibrated per
  physical configuration using simulated replicas as a local
  calibration set. Three closed stages measure robustness to
  ensemble size, to calibration-set size, and to temporal
  horizon. Every stage was frozen before execution, verified
  by abort gates, and closed by a mechanical verdict over
  criteria fixed in advance. The full audit chain — preregistrations,
  freezing minutes, amendments, code and outputs — is anchored by
  SHA-256 and verifiable with the included verifier.
keywords:
  - conformal prediction
  - uncertainty quantification
  - chaotic systems
  - three-body problem
  - preregistration
  - reproducibility
license: Apache-2.0
license-url: >-
  https://github.com/joaquinpenafiel/conformal-prediction-three-body/blob/main/LICENSE
version: 7.7-c
date-released: '2026-09-22'
